At a given temperature, when ionic product \($\left(K_{\text{ip }}\right)\) over comes solubility product \(\left(K_{\text{sp }}\right)\), precipitation of the sparingly soluble electrolyte (here, it is \(\mathrm{CaF}_{2}\) ) takes place.
\(\begin{aligned}
K_{\text{ip }} & =\left[\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}\right] \left[\mathrm{F}^{-}\right]^2=\left(10^{-2}\right)\left(10^{-5}\right)^2=10^{-12}  <  K_{\text{sp }} \\
& =1.6 \times10^{-10}
\end{aligned}\)
So, at this condition \$( \left(10^{-2}  \mathrm{M} \mathrm{Ca}^{2+}+10^{-5}  \mathrm{M} \mathrm{F}^{-}\right)$, precipitation of \( \mathrm{CaF}_2\) will not occur.

